 		"附魔测试盔甲架": "Enchantment Test Armor Stand",
-		"附魔书": "Enchanted Book"
+		"附魔书": "Enchanted Book",
+		"SETTING_MINECRAFT_CLOUDS": "Minecraft Clouds",
+		"流浪商人": "Wandering Trader",
+		"凋灵骷髅": "Wither Skeleton",
+		"石矛": "Stone Spear",
+		"钻石长矛": "Diamond Spear",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_BAT": "Bats latch on and drain enemies, permanently gaining maximum health and healing by actual damage; shields are bitten faster. Feeding on an unshielded target reduces incoming damage and prevents knockback. The swarm periodically merges into a vampire and splits again, preserving total health. The vampire heals twice the drained amount and deals more damage at higher current health.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_JUKEBOX": "Fires sound waves left and right to the music. Channel loudness controls damage, speed, range and spread; each wave hits an enemy once. Consecutive hits increase damage and widen later waves, gaining only one stack per paired volley. A fully missed volley starts gradual stack decay; another hit stops it. Low-frequency waves also cause slight knockback.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_WITHER": "Immune and reflects projectiles while awakening, then explodes. Three heads fire independently; direct and splash damage do not stack on the same victim, and skulls inflict Wither. Charges through enemies, knocking them back and breaking obstacles. At half health, summons a beacon once. Its upward beam deals repeated damage and grants a random Speed, Haste, Resistance or Strength buff when firing begins; the buff ends if the beacon dies.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_WITHER_SKELETON": "Performs two sword slashes, each hitting an enemy once, while moving more slowly. Its smoke-bolt cooldown advances only while the enemy is outside melee range; when ready, it fires a mildly homing bolt. Damaging slashes and bolts apply Wither, or increase its active level and refresh this source duration. Stun, death or disabled attacks cancel unfinished slashes.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_FISHING_ROD": "A cast hook damages and slows; a resting hook can catch passing enemies. Reeling damages enemies along the return path and pulls them in for a sword slash. Also slashes nearby enemies directly and retreats afterward. Casting and slashing share a cooldown; terrain blocks hooks and their return paths.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_SILVERFISH": "Damages enemies on contact. Taking damage or dying agitates nearby stone bricks, hatching allied silverfish up to a family limit of ten. Offspring continue fighting for the same contestant; the entire family must be eliminated.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_GHAST": "Fires fireballs that can be struck back, changing their ownership. Impact explosions deal area damage and knockback without distinguishing friend from foe, can hurt the ghast itself, and destroy breakable terrain.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_BOW": "Slows while drawing; longer draws produce faster arrows and stronger knockback, with damage based on actual arrow speed. Releases early against nearby enemies. Arrows fall under gravity and hit a character only once.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_HAOCHEN": "Each nearby enemy supplies energy while Haochen gradually slows; movement recovers when none remain, without losing stored energy or contributions. A full meter copies the greatest contributor this cycle, breaking ties by earliest contribution. Copies have half size and half common stats except movement speed; skill parameters are unchanged. Existing copies remain. Copies and their descendants cannot target or harm Haochen allies and share his battle survival identity.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_EVOKER": "Summons a line of fangs at range, or several outward-pushing rings nearby; each ring hits a victim once. Periodically replenishes vexes that pass through internal walls and do not expire naturally. A Totem of Undying prevents the first lethal hit and restores health.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_WARDEN": "The shrieker detects enemy movement, collisions and attacks. Full alert launches damaging probes at sound locations; enough returning echoes awaken the Warden and raise health proportionally. It follows the loudest sound, strikes nearby enemies and charges terrain- and shield-piercing sonic knockback attacks at range; stun does not cancel a committed charge. Loud noise briefly boosts speed; prolonged silence causes burrowing and resets alert.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_SKELETON": "Fire rate increases over the battle. Each shot locks its direction when drawing begins. Embedded arrows raise the execution threshold; sufficiently low-health victims trigger an arrow-pull execution. Arrows lodged in obstacles also damage enemies that touch them, then disappear.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_CREEPER": "Nearby enemies build its fuse and slow its movement; the fuse recedes after they leave. A full fuse causes a knockback explosion. Periodic lightning damages and stuns nearby enemies and charges the creeper, shortening its fuse and strengthening and enlarging its blast. After exploding, its head flies off and deals speed-based collision damage, then slows and continues fighting until a second fuse-triggered explosion.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_MINECART": "Lays rails after preparing, then accelerates without a speed cap; powered rails accelerate faster and collision damage rises with speed. Tracks support bends, junctions and loops; replacements change direction but retain powered status. Off-rail movement keeps momentum and collision damage while slowing, and reentry inherits remaining speed. Loops eventually eject the cart. Rails persist for the battle.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_BLAZE": "Fires bursts of fireballs that deal fire damage and inflict burning. Terrain or obstacle impacts leave ground fire that repeatedly damages and ignites enemies. Orbiting rods intercept blockable projectiles that touch them; while attacking, they spread out, spin and damage enemies on contact.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_WANDERING_TRADER": "Brings two leashed llamas that spit at enemies and retaliate after being hit. Leash-pulled llamas deal speed-based collision damage and knockback. Drinks milk only to cleanse negative effects; under threat, uses invisibility or enters a wall and exits at a safer location. A lost llama becomes replaceable after a cooldown, with one returning on the next wall exit. Llamas leave when the trader dies.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_SULFUR_CUBE": "Cycles blocks and retains the latest two traits. Ice lays accelerating trails, removes its own trail speed cap and adds speed-based collision damage. Magma deals fire damage and burning, scorches enemies above and grants fire immunity. Honey briefly grabs and drags without separate damage. Iron reduces damage and speed, leaps and crushes enemies underneath. Amethyst grows independently damaging spikes that can be launched and regrown. TNT explodes, damaging enemies and itself and causing recoil, then consumes its slot and adds a new block. Losing iron redirects movement.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_ENDERMAN": "Can teleport to dodge attacks, with a guaranteed fallback against projectiles; dodges may leave clones. Mutual eye contact and dodging build anger. Rage increases speed and repeatedly teleports it behind enemies to rush them. Continued observation extends rage up to a duration limit.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_OAK_BOAT": "Accelerates to ram enemies and deals paddle damage while turning, with speed affecting damage. Carries up to two characters; the boat and passengers share external damage, while passengers can still attack. With an enemy aboard, it rams walls to hurt hostile passengers. Wall contact reduces speed; destruction releases passengers.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_WOODEN_SWORD": "Longer charges swing faster and deal stronger damage and knockback; ordinary knockback does not interrupt charging. Swinging and taking damage consume durability. At zero durability, hilt and blade fight separately, specializing in knockback and damage. Workbench contact heals and protects fragments; keeping all fragments there rebuilds the sword, combines health and restores durability. Leaving resets progress; a missing fragment or destroyed workbench prevents rebuilding.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_WOODEN_SPEAR": "Movement builds speed. Tip damage scales with its own speed and an enemy approaching head-on; hits accelerate it, with larger gains from aligned hits. High-speed piercing briefly boosts speed; straight-through attacks hit harder but consume more stored speed. Its tip blocks and removes blockable projectiles. Walls slow it down; stun resets speed.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_DROWNED": "Throws tridents through characters and retrieves them; wall impacts lodge the trident and eventually trigger a replacement. Held or lodged tridents become enchanted over time, summoning damaging, stunning lightning that can charge other eligible tridents. Charged contact calls another strike. Allied eligible tridents periodically connect into an electric network that damages and briefly stuns enemies.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_WITCH": "Brews random buffs, healing, damage or debuff potions. Usually drinks beneficial potions and throws harmful ones, but can make mistakes. At high health it does not brew healing potions. Against enemies with inverted healing and damage, it adjusts potion use; if all enemies are inverted, the healing restriction is removed. Thrown potions apply their respective effects around impact.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_SHULKER": "Moves along floors and side walls. Closing its shell slows movement and blocks damage; opening it fires homing levitation bullets. Volley size grows with battle time. Taking damage while open can trigger a teleport to safety.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_ELYTRA_SPEAR": "Glides with firework boosts; spear-tip damage rises with flight speed. Low-speed pokes retreat afterward, while high-speed hits pierce and grant larger speed boosts. Alignment enables a piercing dash followed by a turn back. Automatically steers back when outside the arena.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_ELYTRA_MACE": "Glides with firework boosts and dives to strike nearby enemies. Hits launch a chain of rebound slams, increasing height, area, damage and knockback until a miss or interruption. Steers back from outside the arena without cancelling a committed chain merely because it is returning.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_ELYTRA_MACE_SPEAR": "Flies with firework boosts and deals speed-based spear damage. Low-speed pokes retreat; high-speed piercing gains more speed on hit. Hits also cause an area mace strike and begin rebound slams. A piercing dash completes before the leap; chained slams increase area and damage until a miss or interruption. Arena-return steering does not cancel a committed chain.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_STONE_SPEAR": "Actual movement permanently builds speed for the battle. Four copies periodically switch between following, orbiting and thrusting formations. Higher speed tightens the following formation, accelerates orbit and extends thrusts. Only moving tips deal speed-based damage; idle and retracting thrusts are harmless. In orbit formation, only the four copy tips block and remove blockable projectiles, not shafts or gaps.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_SLIME": "Damages enemies during jumps; landings deal area damage and slow. Death causes a damaging knockback pulse and splits it into two smaller slimes, except at the smallest stage. All descendants continue fighting for the original contestant.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_GUARDIAN": "Locks on and charges a high-damage laser; other enemies crossing its beam also take damage and are pushed sideways. Nearby enemies trigger a charged spike burst, with repeated contact damage while extended. Actual damage received delays laser and spike attacks, with larger hits causing longer delays.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_MOSS_BLOCK": "Periodically spreads stackable moss. Each touched cell has independent damage and cooldown; deeper layers deal more damage, while only the strongest contacted slow applies. Contact heals the owner without consuming moss. Connected moss enables a burrowing ambush at the enemy position recorded on entry, dealing damage and knockback and consuming nearby moss to heal. Moss persists without blocking movement but can be destroyed by ghast explosions; blocked or destroyed exits cancel ambushes.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_LONGBOW_OF_THE_HEAVENS": "Charges homing arrows that pass through terrain, trigger area arrow rain on impact and leave rifts; the arrow itself causes no knockback. On an incoming hit, an available rift can be consumed to dodge and teleport with transit immunity. Arrival causes repeated outward damage and knockback. Dodging requires a safe rift and a ready cooldown.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_BLACKSMITH_VILLAGER": "Slashes nearby enemies and forges while idle. Longer periods without attacking accelerate forging, including time spent stunned. Every few forging cycles randomly upgrades the sword or helmet, increasing damage or protection. After equipment is fully upgraded, further forging permanently improves damage or armor.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_IRON_GOLEM": "Charges an uppercut; longer charges increase damage and launch strength and briefly stun enemies. Its accompanying villager repairs health. If the villager dies, permanent rage increases damage, movement speed and attack speed.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_ANVIL": "Obeys gravity, leaps toward enemies and keeps tracking horizontally; faster falls deal more damage. The jump passes through characters but remains vulnerable, and terrain contact triggers an immediate slam. Enemy hits do not stop the fall; continued underside contact crushes and pushes victims, unlike side or top contact. A hit allows another slam after landing, with no chain-count limit; a miss starts the cooldown.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_COPPER_SWORD": "Consecutive hits accelerate sword swings, which slightly slow movement. A miss, interruption or long gap between hits resets the speed bonus. Rust builds over time; when fully rusted, a natural lightning strike clears rust and negative effects and charges the sword, preserving buffs. Lightning damages and stuns enemies. Charged melee hits also call lightning, but these attack strikes do not cleanse.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_FOG_MAN": "Fog limits vision to nearby space and facing direction, with walls blocking sight. Stealth prevents automatic targeting but not area hits. Prolonged exposure costs health and disperses it before it reappears, preferably out of sight. Successful flanking warns of lightning and triggers rage, alternating retreat with mist pass-through attacks or area ambushes. Mist form remains vulnerable but avoids exposure health loss; rage is followed by a cooldown.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_CACTUS": "Periodically grows taller up to a layer limit, enlarging its body; only its sides deal contact damage. Fires thorns to both sides, with more thorns at greater height. Actual damage received triggers retaliation whose total scales with damage taken and height. Each thorn hits once and causes no continuing damage after lodging in a target or wall.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_SNOW_GOLEM": "Snowballs damage, slightly knock back and build cold. Full snow trails repeatedly damage and chill, then become harmless while melting away. Cold slows movement and attacks; a full meter briefly freezes the victim in breakable ice. Normal attacks can trigger a twenty-shot spread volley. Reaching half health guarantees one volley; if already firing one, the guarantee carries to the next attack.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_SHEEP": "Spends wool to repel nearby enemies and incoming projectiles; being shorn increases speed. Charge damage and knockback scale with impact speed. Resists knockback while preparing and charging; fast wall crashes cause self-damage and stun. At low health, a period without damage allows stationary grazing that heals and regrows wool. Taking damage interrupts grazing; full health ends it.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_ALLAY": "Continuously generates notes, gaining faster generation and higher capacity over time. Notes home toward enemies and can collect incoming projectiles to send back. Nearby enemies trigger recall of flying notes, which spiral inward before an area damage and knockback burst. Captured cargo has limited capacity; returned projectiles retain their original attack properties.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_STICKY_PISTON": "Repeatedly extends forward. Its head can hold enemies while the front spike damages them; unheld targets are pushed away and can be stunned against walls. Sustained attacking speeds up the strokes while slowing its own movement; the buildup fades after stopping.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_SPIDER": "Anchors silk to walls, forming a hunting network of strands and webs at intersections. Silk and web contact damage and slow enemies, with stronger slowing in webs. Enemies caught in webs trigger a damaging lunge; walls block its hit.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_MACE": "A successful close-range swing launches a leap and ground slam, dealing area damage and knockback. Further hits trigger rebound slams with increasing height, area, damage and knockback. Height and area are capped, but successful chains can keep increasing damage. A miss or interruption ends the sequence.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_DIAMOND_SWORD": "Slashes nearby enemies and sends a sweeping attack forward. After obtaining a netherite ingot, touching a smithing table starts a stationary upgrade to a netherite sword, increasing current and maximum health, damage and attack speed. Leaving the table interrupts the wait.",
+		"MC_ARMOR_INTRO_DIAMOND_SPEAR": "Movement builds speed, turning loses it, and hits restore more. Speed increases thrust damage and echo count; fast echoes upgrade to piercing attacks. Frontal thrusts trigger fixed-position echo volleys, while side attacks sweep a half-circle with knockback. A frontal target and clear path allow a prepared blink-pierce with echoes."
 	}
 }
